<h3>2.4 Shortcomings of Presently Available Solutions</h3>

<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Solution</th>
    <th>Shortcomings</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><b>BlaBlaCar</b></td>
    <td>Focused exclusively on intercity travel; no support for daily intra-city commuting; no coin-based reward system; limited real-time route visualization; no open-source monitoring stack</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><b>QuickRide</b></td>
    <td>Proprietary closed-source platform; limited amenity-based filtering; no government ID verification system; ride matching lacks interactive map-based source/destination selection</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><b>sRide</b></td>
    <td>Restricted to corporate users only; no public registration; no multi-level verification (email + phone + govt ID); no admin panel for platform governance</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><b>Existing Research</b></td>
    <td>Optimization models remain largely theoretical; lack end-to-end implementation with production-grade security (OAuth2), caching (Caffeine), containerization (Docker), and observability (Prometheus + Grafana)</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h3>2.5 Idea of Proposed Solution</h3>

<p><b>RideX</b> proposes a comprehensive, production-ready carpooling platform that addresses all identified shortcomings through the following novel contributions:</p>

<ol>
  <li><b>Multi-Level Identity Verification:</b> Unlike existing platforms that rely on phone-only verification, RideX implements a three-tier verification system — email token verification, phone OTP verification, and admin-reviewed government ID verification (Aadhaar/PAN) — establishing a trust score visible on user profiles.</li>
  <li><b>Interactive Map-Based Ride Creation &amp; Visualization:</b> Rides are created by selecting source and destination directly on an interactive Leaflet.js map. The OSRM routing engine computes the optimal route polyline, distance, and estimated duration in real-time, displayed as an overlay on OpenStreetMap tiles — a feature absent in most competing platforms.</li>
  <li><b>Coin-Based Gamification Engine:</b> A novel reward system where drivers earn <code>(distance × 0.10) + 5</code> bonus coins per completed ride, and co-riders earn <code>(distance × 0.10)</code> coins. Accumulated coins can be redeemed as discounts on future bookings, incentivizing repeated platform usage and improving rider retention.</li>
  <li><b>Amenity-Based Ride Filtering:</b> Beyond basic source/destination/date search, riders can filter by AC availability, luggage space, pet-friendliness, smoking policy, time of day, price range, and driver rating — enabling precise ride matching aligned with passenger preferences.</li>
  <li><b>Production-Grade Observability:</b> Full Prometheus + Grafana monitoring stack deployed via Docker Compose, scraping JVM metrics, HTTP request latencies, database connection pool statistics, and custom business metrics — a capability typically found only in enterprise applications, not in academic projects.</li>
  <li><b>Automated Ride Lifecycle Management:</b> A scheduled task (running every 20 minutes) automatically transitions rides through PLANNED → ONGOING → COMPLETED states based on timestamp comparison, and triggers coin disbursement upon completion — eliminating manual status management.</li>
</ol>

<hr class="section-divider">

<!-- ===================== SECTION 3 ===================== -->
<h2>3. Module-Wise Description (Major Features)</h2>

<h3>Module 1: Authentication &amp; Authorization Module <i>(Core)</i></h3>
<ul>
  <li>Form-based login with email/password (BCrypt-encrypted password hashing)</li>
  <li>OAuth2 social login integration (Google and GitHub providers)</li>
  <li>Role-based access control with two roles: <code>USER</code> and <code>ADMIN</code></li>
  <li>Email verification via secure, time-limited token-based flow</li>
  <li>Password reset via OTP delivered through SMTP email service</li>
  <li>Remember-me functionality with 24-hour token validity</li>
  <li>Custom authentication success/failure handlers for role-based redirects</li>
</ul>

<h3>Module 2: User Profile &amp; Vehicle Registration Module</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Profile creation and editing — name, photo, bio, travel preferences</li>
  <li>Profile picture upload to Cloudinary cloud storage</li>
  <li>Travel preferences configuration — music, pets, smoking, chattiness</li>
  <li>Spoken languages, occupation, city information</li>
  <li>Ride statistics tracking — completed rides, cancelled rides, last ride date</li>
  <li>Vehicle (car) registration with make, model, year, type, color, plate number</li>
  <li>Fuel type specification, seat capacity, AC availability</li>
  <li>Multi-image upload for vehicle photos via Cloudinary</li>
</ul>

<h3>Module 3: Multi-Level User Verification Module <i>(Innovative)</i></h3>
<ul>
  <li><b>Level 1 — Email Verification:</b> Token-based email confirmation sent via Spring Mail SMTP</li>
  <li><b>Level 2 — Phone Verification:</b> OTP-based phone number verification</li>
  <li><b>Level 3 — Government ID Verification:</b> User uploads Aadhaar/PAN document; admin reviews and approves/rejects the verification request through the admin panel</li>
  <li>Verification status badges displayed prominently on user profiles, building platform trust</li>
</ul>

<h3>Module 4: Ride Management &amp; Route Visualization Module <i>(Innovative)</i></h3>
<ul>
  <li><b>Create Ride:</b> Publish a ride with map-based source/destination selection, date/time picker, per-seat pricing, available seats, and amenity tags</li>
  <li><b>Route Computation:</b> OSRM API integration for real-time distance, duration, and optimal route polyline calculation</li>
  <li><b>Interactive Map Display:</b> Leaflet.js + OpenStreetMap with route polyline overlay, source/destination markers, and zoom controls</li>
  <li><b>Search Ride:</b> Filter by source city, destination city, travel date</li>
  <li><b>Advanced Filters:</b> Price range slider, amenities (AC, luggage, pets, smoking), time of day, minimum driver rating</li>
  <li><b>Ride Status Lifecycle:</b> Automated state machine — <code>PLANNED</code> → <code>ONGOING</code> → <code>COMPLETED</code> — managed by a Spring <code>@Scheduled</code> task running every 20 minutes</li>
</ul>

<h3>Module 5: Booking, Coin Reward &amp; Rating Module <i>(Innovative)</i></h3>
<ul>
  <li><b>Ride Booking:</b> Passengers request to join a ride, specifying seat count; option to volunteer as co-driver</li>
  <li><b>Coin Discount:</b> Passengers can apply earned coins as a price discount during booking</li>
  <li><b>Driver Decision:</b> Driver reviews and approves or rejects each booking request</li>
  <li><b>Email Notifications:</b> Automated email sent to passenger on booking approval/rejection</li>
  <li><b>Coin Reward Engine:</b>
    <ul>
      <li>Driver earns: <code>(distance × 0.10) + 5 bonus</code> coins per completed ride</li>
      <li>Co-rider earns: <code>(distance × 0.10)</code> coins per completed ride</li>
      <li>Coins accumulate in user wallet and are redeemable on future bookings</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><b>Rating System:</b> Post-ride star rating (1–5 stars) with text review; average rating computed and displayed on user profiles</li>
</ul>

<h3>Module 6: Admin Panel &amp; System Monitoring Module</h3>
<ul>
  <li><b>Admin Dashboard:</b> Platform-wide statistics (total users, total rides, active rides, pending verifications)</li>
  <li><b>User Management:</b> View all users, search by name/email, manage accounts</li>
  <li><b>Ride Management:</b> View all rides with status filters and search capability</li>
  <li><b>Government ID Review:</b> Admin reviews uploaded ID documents and approves or rejects verification requests</li>
  <li><b>Prometheus Metrics:</b> JVM metrics, HTTP request metrics, DB connection pool metrics exposed at <code>/actuator/prometheus</code></li>
  <li><b>Grafana Dashboards:</b> Real-time visualization of system health, request latencies, and resource utilization</li>
  <li><b>Docker Compose Deployment:</b> Four-service containerized stack (MySQL, Spring Boot App, Prometheus, Grafana)</li>
</ul>

