<h3>4.2 System Data Flow Diagram</h3>

<div class="er-note">
  <p><b>Note:</b> The System Data Flow Diagram is best viewed in the original Markdown file (<code>SYNOPSIS.md</code>) which renders the Mermaid diagram interactively. A textual description of the data flow is provided below.</p>
</div>

<h4>Data Flow Summary:</h4>

<p>The system architecture follows a layered MVC pattern with the following data flow:</p>

<ul>
  <li><b>User/Driver</b> interacts with the system through six controllers: Auth Controller, User Controller, Ride Controller, Search Controller, Admin Controller, and Rating Controller.</li>
  <li><b>Controllers</b> delegate business logic to service layer components: User Service, Ride Service, Detail Service, Image Service, Cache Service, Ride Request Service, and Rating Service.</li>
  <li><b>Services</b> interact with:
    <ul>
      <li><b>MySQL 8.0 Database</b> — for persistent data storage</li>
      <li><b>Email Service (SMTP)</b> — for verification emails and booking notifications</li>
      <li><b>Cloudinary (Image CDN)</b> — for profile and vehicle image storage</li>
      <li><b>OSRM (Route Engine)</b> — for real-time route computation</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><b>Monitoring:</b> Prometheus scrapes metrics from <code>/actuator/prometheus</code>, and Grafana visualizes the collected metrics.</li>
</ul>

