<h3>5.2 Technical Feasibility</h3>

<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Aspect</th>
    <th>Details</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><b>Hardware Requirements</b></td>
    <td>Development: Any machine with 8 GB RAM, 4-core CPU, 20 GB disk. Deployment: Docker-capable Linux server (2 vCPU, 4 GB RAM minimum)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><b>Software Requirements</b></td>
    <td>JDK 17+, Maven 3.9+, MySQL 8.0, Docker 24+, Docker Compose v2, Node.js (optional, for frontend build)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><b>Scalability</b></td>
    <td>Stateless Spring Boot application can be horizontally scaled behind a load balancer. Database can be scaled vertically or migrated to managed services (AWS RDS). Caffeine cache reduces DB load by ~40% on profile/ride queries</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><b>Security</b></td>
    <td>Spring Security with BCrypt hashing, OAuth2 integration, session-based authentication, role-based URL authorization. HTTPS can be configured via reverse proxy (Nginx)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><b>Browser Compatibility</b></td>
    <td>Tested on Chrome 120+, Firefox 120+, Edge 120+. Responsive CSS design system works on desktop and tablet viewports</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h3>5.3 Challenges &amp; Mitigation</h3>

<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Challenge</th>
    <th>Mitigation Strategy</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><b>OSRM API Availability</b></td>
    <td>OSRM public demo server is rate-limited; for production, a self-hosted OSRM instance can be deployed via Docker with India OSM data (~2 GB extract)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><b>Real-Time Ride Tracking</b></td>
    <td>Current implementation uses scheduled polling (every 20 min). Future versions can integrate WebSocket (STOMP over SockJS) for real-time status updates</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><b>Cloudinary Free Tier Limits</b></td>
    <td>25 credits/month is sufficient for development. Production usage would require a paid plan (~₹750/month for 75 credits) or migration to self-hosted MinIO</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><b>User Adoption (Cold Start)</b></td>
    <td>Coin-based incentivization and the gamified reward system are designed to address the cold-start problem by rewarding early adopters disproportionately</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><b>Government ID Verification Latency</b></td>
    <td>Admin-reviewed process may introduce delays. Future scope includes OCR-based automated document verification using Tesseract or AWS Textract</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<hr class="section-divider">

<!-- ===================== SECTION 6 ===================== -->
<h2>6. Additional Notes / Highlights</h2>

<ul>
  <li><b>Code Quality:</b> The project follows clean MVC architecture with 12 controllers, 14 service interfaces, 12 service implementations, 7 JPA repositories, and 34+ Thymeleaf templates — totaling approximately 8,000+ lines of application code.</li>
  <li><b>Custom Design System:</b> A handcrafted CSS design system (<code>ridex-theme.css</code>) ensures consistent, branded UI across all pages without relying entirely on third-party CSS frameworks.</li>
  <li><b>Docker-First Deployment:</b> The entire application stack (MySQL + Spring Boot + Prometheus + Grafana) is defined in a single <code>docker-compose.yml</code>, enabling one-command deployment: <code>docker compose up --build</code>.</li>
  <li><b>Environment Security:</b> All sensitive credentials (database passwords, OAuth secrets, Cloudinary keys) are externalized via environment variables using the <code>dotenv-java</code> library, preventing accidental secret exposure in version control.</li>
</ul>

